WEBVTT

00:01.840 --> 00:04.240
Old man Zohei mentioned it to me...

00:04.240 --> 00:08.730
Apparently Hyoma's first real fight 
happened when he was twelve.

00:07.730 --> 00:08.730
<b>Wild Caught in the North Sea
Dried Squid</b>

00:08.730 --> 00:10.230
<b>Wild Caught in the North Sea
Dried Squid</b>

00:08.730 --> 00:10.230
<b>Greengrocer
Noriki</b>

00:09.040 --> 00:10.230
Twelve?

00:10.790 --> 00:14.840
His hatred of tsukumogami 
spurred him to look up some info,

00:14.840 --> 00:15.870
run off on his own,

00:16.280 --> 00:19.690
and risk his life hunting down tsukumogami.

00:20.370 --> 00:23.620
<b>Dried Goods</b>

00:20.370 --> 00:23.620
<b>Sugitora</b>

00:21.720 --> 00:23.620
"The Onigawara of Ou."

00:24.030 --> 00:27.630
That's a tsukumogami they had up there, 
about as powerful as us.

00:28.340 --> 00:32.510
Hyoma destroyed the thing at eighteen.

00:32.710 --> 00:34.020
What?!

00:34.330 --> 00:36.220
Totally stupid, right?

00:36.220 --> 00:37.510
I could hardly believe it.

00:37.510 --> 00:41.660
But he survived that desperate battle.

00:42.750 --> 00:44.640
Hyoma's damn strong.

01:00.960 --> 01:03.160
Well, Representative Kadomori?

01:04.440 --> 01:05.660
Is that everything?

01:17.840 --> 01:25.600
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

02:39.010 --> 02:44.010
<b>Circumstances</b>

02:50.660 --> 02:52.110
Curious.

02:52.110 --> 02:54.260
What'd I say before?

02:56.040 --> 02:59.930
Big moves like that must 
tire him out pretty fast.

03:00.650 --> 03:01.780
Hold it.

03:02.780 --> 03:05.410
Let's play a bit longer.

03:11.300 --> 03:12.470
There's more?

03:16.150 --> 03:17.090
You're...

03:20.050 --> 03:21.130
Yagen!

03:21.220 --> 03:23.340
<b>— Yagen —</b>

03:24.500 --> 03:28.100
<i>Guess it was worth hitting 
him with that curveball.</i>

03:28.100 --> 03:32.100
<i>See? I really do use 
every resource available.</i>

03:34.770 --> 03:35.670
I see.

03:36.110 --> 03:40.280
After I left you, you were placed 
in the service of the Kyoto Saenome.

03:40.960 --> 03:44.220
I never thought I'd meet you again like this.

03:45.150 --> 03:46.020
Yagen...

03:50.270 --> 03:56.090
"Tsukumogami are not people, 
but should be used like the objects they are"?

03:56.570 --> 04:00.130
You Kadomoris see tsukumogami 
as tools and nothing more, then?

04:00.950 --> 04:03.510
You think it's gross? We hear that a lot.

04:03.510 --> 04:07.340
Well, the custom has let you 
keep Kyoto safe, hasn't it?

04:07.340 --> 04:09.210
That's an admirable thing.

04:09.210 --> 04:13.020
And Kadomori-san is 
unflinching in his belief.

04:13.360 --> 04:15.580
People like that are very strong.

04:17.030 --> 04:19.020
Strong, huh?

04:41.080 --> 04:43.590
He's not as sharp as he was before, eh?

04:43.590 --> 04:45.590
<i>I thought so.</i>

04:46.110 --> 04:48.310
I have developed a fondness for that family.

04:49.370 --> 04:52.650
<i>Explains why he didn't speak 
solely of Nagatsuki Botan,</i>

04:52.650 --> 04:56.010
<i>but of that tsukumogami "family."</i>

04:56.560 --> 05:01.850
<i>The brat's developed 
sympathies for tsukumogami.</i>

05:02.320 --> 05:05.820
<i>At least, he's starting to.</i>

05:06.710 --> 05:09.410
<i>He's every bit the fighter 
I heard, of course.</i>

05:09.740 --> 05:13.290
<i>The blade of hatred knows no mercy.</i>

05:13.700 --> 05:17.640
<i>But set a familiar face after him, 
and suddenly he's wracked with doubt...</i>

05:18.290 --> 05:20.350
<i>Zohei...</i>

05:20.350 --> 05:25.670
<i>You sent the boy here to understand 
tsukumogami better and grow in the process.</i>

05:25.670 --> 05:28.460
<i>It backfired on you.</i>

05:28.460 --> 05:30.280
<i>It's made him fragile.</i>

05:34.280 --> 05:36.140
<i>Hey, kiddo...</i>

05:36.890 --> 05:39.910
<i>If you lose here, 
I'm gonna take you into custody.</i>

05:40.400 --> 05:43.320
<i>And even if you do finish off Yagen...</i>

05:43.320 --> 05:47.160
<i>While your mind's gone blank from destroying 
something you had tender feelings for,</i>

05:47.160 --> 05:50.400
<i>I'll hit you with a control talisman.</i>

05:50.400 --> 05:52.230
<i>It'll be hard to fight that one.</i>

05:57.200 --> 06:00.960
Yagen, you've had more than your 
share of misfortune, haven't you?

06:08.400 --> 06:09.470
<i>Yes.</i>

06:09.470 --> 06:11.270
<i>There's the right choice to make.</i>

06:11.720 --> 06:14.470
<i>They're only objects, after all.</i>

06:14.470 --> 06:17.450
<i>But I've won the day!</i>

06:32.490 --> 06:34.910
Well? What's next?!

06:34.910 --> 06:37.250
<i>H-How...</i>

06:37.750 --> 06:40.780
<i>How's he still so calm?!</i>

06:45.460 --> 06:46.900
<i>What?</i>

06:50.070 --> 06:51.510
<i>I...</i>

06:51.800 --> 06:53.790
<i>He saved it?!</i>

06:53.790 --> 06:57.910
<i>That's why he let it get close enough 
to put himself in danger of a hit,</i>

06:58.270 --> 07:01.770
<i>so he could strip the talisman off its face?!</i>

07:02.260 --> 07:04.270
What happened to my clothes?!

07:05.160 --> 07:06.460
Why?

07:07.730 --> 07:10.000
You didn't have to save it.

07:10.000 --> 07:14.270
Why'd you choose the toughest 
way around the problem?

07:14.270 --> 07:15.780
That's an absurd question.

07:16.060 --> 07:17.190
It was instinct.

07:18.040 --> 07:20.120
Instinct told me that that was the only way.

07:20.120 --> 07:21.750
I followed that instinct.

07:25.400 --> 07:28.460
The old, "Don't think, feel," huh?

07:28.460 --> 07:30.800
He's just like they told me.

07:31.370 --> 07:33.550
<i>We've got someone like that 
in our family, too.</i>

07:34.370 --> 07:37.450
He just barrels forward in 
the direction he believes in,

07:37.450 --> 07:40.790
halfway between foolish and valiant.

07:41.350 --> 07:44.610
But he's unflinching in 
every belief he's ever held.

07:45.490 --> 07:47.360
Is he your...

07:47.360 --> 07:51.880
Yeah. He's our little brother, Hyoma.

07:52.830 --> 07:55.550
Papa, can we be done for now?

07:55.550 --> 07:58.760
My brothers lost all their pieces, 
so it's kind of a stalemate.

07:59.120 --> 08:01.870
You stay out of this, Tsubaki!

08:02.160 --> 08:04.170
Now, Papa...

08:04.170 --> 08:06.880
If you escalate things any further...

08:08.730 --> 08:11.510
I might be forced to take Hyoma-chan's side.

08:13.790 --> 08:14.900
Formation talismans?

08:15.710 --> 08:18.890
I've grown to like him, see?

08:20.230 --> 08:23.220
Another unruly child, eh?

08:25.650 --> 08:28.270
Matsu, get up already!

08:29.810 --> 08:32.030
You too, Tsubaki. Get Ume up.

08:32.410 --> 08:33.400
All right!

08:37.350 --> 08:39.880
What now, Representative Kadomori?

08:39.880 --> 08:41.830
What do you think?

08:43.140 --> 08:45.210
I might've overdone it a bit.

08:45.210 --> 08:46.200
You passed!

08:46.200 --> 08:48.090
You passed with flying colors, Hyoma-kun!

08:49.110 --> 08:52.460
While I gave you permission to operate, 
I wanted to test you a bit, as well.

08:52.850 --> 08:54.780
And while I might've been 
trying to test your power,

08:54.780 --> 08:57.820
I probably got a little too mean 
about Nagatsuki-san in the process!

08:57.820 --> 09:00.350
But now I can see the whole picture.

09:00.350 --> 09:04.200
You've got strength and resolve in spades!

09:04.200 --> 09:06.480
I think you'll get by in this town.

09:14.770 --> 09:17.560
I-Is that what it was about?

09:18.660 --> 09:20.240
<i>Simpleton.</i>

09:20.720 --> 09:22.870
I'll let you take custody of Yagen.

09:22.870 --> 09:25.500
She'll be under Kunato jurisdiction now.

09:27.510 --> 09:28.540
Hyoma-kun...

09:29.850 --> 09:32.500
You're an interesting one.

09:32.880 --> 09:34.950
Hope to see more of you.

09:36.370 --> 09:37.260
Hey.

09:38.290 --> 09:40.040
You owe me one for today.

09:40.040 --> 09:41.890
Drop me a line sometime.

09:41.890 --> 09:44.890
We'll have a nice, long talk...

09:45.320 --> 09:48.310
Reminiscing about Hayato-san and Kusui-san.

09:50.630 --> 09:51.770
You're...

09:52.690 --> 09:53.930
Tsubaki.

09:53.930 --> 09:55.900
Kadomori Tsubaki.

09:55.900 --> 09:56.780
Later!

10:01.880 --> 10:02.660
Excuse me.

10:03.330 --> 10:05.160
Do you know what's going on here?

10:05.580 --> 10:08.290
And... what should I do?

10:08.750 --> 10:11.180
I'll explain everything on the way.

10:11.180 --> 10:13.660
For now, come along.

10:15.160 --> 10:16.410
Hang on!

10:16.410 --> 10:18.410
Kushige fell asleep in the bath?!

10:18.410 --> 10:21.690
Yeah, apparently he's been drinking for days.

10:21.690 --> 10:23.320
Haori, look after him!

10:23.320 --> 10:26.410
Yu, a change of clothes! Kagami, wet a towel!

10:26.410 --> 10:29.060
Hey, Botan! Do I smell something burning?

10:29.520 --> 10:31.420
Kushige's back, then?

10:31.820 --> 10:34.800
What is this? A den of iniquity?

10:34.800 --> 10:37.630
Why would you say that? 
It's the Nagatsuki estate.

10:37.630 --> 10:39.570
The demon castle of 
those tsukumogami-hunters?!

10:40.770 --> 10:42.700
You still believe that?

10:43.310 --> 10:45.320
I contacted the Kunato.

10:45.320 --> 10:47.700
Someone will be by to get you tomorrow.

10:48.200 --> 10:50.710
You'll only have to stay here one night.

10:52.210 --> 10:54.840
Oh! Welcome back, Hyoma-san!

10:55.540 --> 10:57.130
Why are you all wrecked?!

10:57.130 --> 10:59.020
No reason.

10:59.020 --> 11:01.160
H-Hold on a minute!

11:02.960 --> 11:06.260
Who wouldn't want to get rid of it?

11:06.260 --> 11:07.340
<i>Those eyes...</i>

11:07.770 --> 11:10.810
<i>I don't know exactly 
how far he intended to go,</i>

11:10.810 --> 11:13.620
<i>but his eyes, in that moment, 
were completely sincere.</i>

11:15.190 --> 11:18.900
Children and adults both 
gave Botan a wide berth.

11:18.900 --> 11:22.170
<i>Nagatsuki-san's been subjected 
to that all her life.</i>

11:31.800 --> 11:32.840
Sorry.

11:32.840 --> 11:36.400
It's just, you always seem to 
come back a little beat up.

11:36.400 --> 11:39.130
You're like some rambunctious little kid.

11:40.390 --> 11:42.380
Well? Come inside.

11:44.130 --> 11:45.140
What's wrong?

11:46.500 --> 11:47.640
Nothing.

11:48.930 --> 11:52.770
The sight of your face 
seems to have set me at ease.

11:53.680 --> 11:57.270
Uh... Um... Huh?

11:57.270 --> 11:59.830
Forgive me. It's nothing.

12:00.320 --> 12:01.860
Anyway, Yagen!

12:04.110 --> 12:05.530
Forgive me, Nagatsuki-san.

12:06.040 --> 12:09.210
Would it be possible to 
house her here for a day?

12:12.730 --> 12:15.260
<i>Tattered clothing... Injuries...</i>

12:16.040 --> 12:19.850
<i>Clothing messed up... 
Beautiful girl who looks scared...</i>

12:25.760 --> 12:27.770
I merely took pity on an unfortunate woman!

12:26.400 --> 12:27.770
<i>Explain the situation.</i>

12:27.770 --> 12:30.220
Such a martyr.

12:30.220 --> 12:31.560
My clothing...

12:31.560 --> 12:33.290
<i>Look after Kushige.</i>

12:34.200 --> 12:35.340
Drink!

12:34.850 --> 12:38.770
<i>And a welcome party for Yagen... 
as a pretense for drinking.</i>

12:35.340 --> 12:37.750
And give me your email address!

12:38.770 --> 12:41.690
So Yagen-san will be heading out tomorrow?

12:40.310 --> 12:43.910
<i>And tomorrow's the deadline for my report...</i>

12:41.690 --> 12:42.490
Indeed.

12:42.490 --> 12:44.390
Wanna drink? Let's drink!

12:45.760 --> 12:48.410
What? You finished it?

12:49.520 --> 12:52.540
I guess yesterday's hub-bub 
helped to clear my head!

12:52.880 --> 12:55.600
The others all went shopping.

12:55.600 --> 12:57.630
Suzuri wanted to buy clothes.

12:57.630 --> 12:58.520
What about you?

12:58.520 --> 13:01.420
I need to tend to Kushige, of course.

13:01.420 --> 13:02.860
I see!

13:02.860 --> 13:05.430
Nagatsuki-san, I'm heading out now.

13:05.430 --> 13:08.720
Huh? Oh... to see off Yagen-san?

13:08.720 --> 13:13.060
Yes. There's a place she wanted 
to visit before she leaves,

13:13.060 --> 13:14.790
so we're leaving a bit early.

13:14.790 --> 13:16.060
Oh...

13:16.960 --> 13:18.440
Hey, Botan.

13:18.440 --> 13:20.320
Why don't you go with them?

13:20.320 --> 13:21.160
Huh?

13:21.160 --> 13:23.190
I really think you should.

13:23.600 --> 13:26.700
Think about the situation Hyoma-san's in.

13:27.040 --> 13:30.200
Heading out <i>alone</i> with a beautiful woman...

13:30.590 --> 13:31.950
What could such things lead to?!

13:34.050 --> 13:36.800
Please accompany me, Nagatsuki-san.

13:36.800 --> 13:39.340
I wish there to be no doubts 
about the situation.

13:40.080 --> 13:44.020
Well... I'd really appreciate 
you coming with me.

13:44.490 --> 13:46.200
His eyes are so scary.

13:47.210 --> 13:48.580
<i>Yeah, I get that.</i>

13:49.920 --> 13:53.020
Maybe I'll just do that, then.

13:55.020 --> 14:00.060
I feel like I once spent 
a great deal of time there,

14:00.350 --> 14:02.570
as a tool with its master.

14:04.110 --> 14:06.740
I'd like to see it once before I go.

14:07.410 --> 14:09.140
Your vessel's memories?

14:11.010 --> 14:13.080
Yes, most likely...

14:13.440 --> 14:15.740
But it's like a memory from a past life,

14:15.740 --> 14:19.070
so while I have strong attachments 
to my hometown and my master,

14:19.070 --> 14:23.770
I can't clearly summon 
its location, or his face.

14:24.410 --> 14:26.840
<i>Marebito are like lost children.</i>

14:28.070 --> 14:29.560
It's a difficult issue.

14:29.560 --> 14:34.350
You rarely hear of a tsukumogami 
so influenced by its vessel.

14:34.670 --> 14:40.440
Do you think that going there 
will trigger some memories for you?

14:40.440 --> 14:42.610
That seems unlikely.

14:43.180 --> 14:47.640
My time as a mere mortar wheel 
was likely centuries ago.

14:48.560 --> 14:51.050
There's likely no trace left.

14:51.050 --> 14:53.920
Sorry I asked such a stupid question.

14:53.920 --> 14:55.370
Oh, it's fine...

14:55.850 --> 14:59.500
I can't even be sure 
that this is where it was.

15:00.260 --> 15:04.970
Before I became a special exception, 
I visited it several times out of curiosity...

15:06.210 --> 15:08.710
But I never learned anything.

15:09.770 --> 15:13.280
The feelings of comfort felt by the 
mortar wheel that became your vessel

15:13.280 --> 15:15.300
transferred into you.

15:16.430 --> 15:18.680
<i>That's why I wanted to know...</i>

15:18.680 --> 15:22.560
<i>If the source of those outpouring emotions, 
and the one toward whom they were felt,</i>

15:23.280 --> 15:25.400
<i>really existed.</i>

15:27.030 --> 15:30.200
Yes, I suppose there's nothing here.

15:31.010 --> 15:32.700
But please hear me, my master...

15:33.430 --> 15:38.730
Because of you, your mortar wheel 
truly loves the world of the living.

15:38.730 --> 15:39.770
Thank you.

15:43.240 --> 15:44.670
Have you had enough?

15:44.670 --> 15:46.680
Yes, more than enough.

15:46.680 --> 15:47.710
And...

15:47.710 --> 15:52.220
I'd hate to take up any more 
of the happy couple's time.

15:52.220 --> 15:53.470
What?!

15:54.520 --> 15:56.970
Well, I was told that you were engaged.

15:56.970 --> 15:58.110
No!

15:58.110 --> 16:01.070
That engagement stuff is 
all Haori and the others' idea!

16:01.070 --> 16:04.730
Indeed! Nagatsuki-san and I do
 not yet have any such relationship!

16:04.730 --> 16:05.390
<i>Yet</i>?!

16:05.390 --> 16:06.700
Wh-What did I say?!

16:09.200 --> 16:12.990
The Kunatos have a similar rule about their 
special exceptions needing to work,

16:13.590 --> 16:17.200
but it won't be as unilateral 
as it was with the Kadomoris.

16:17.200 --> 16:19.850
If you'd rather return to the land 
of the dead, tell them that.

16:21.050 --> 16:23.120
Please, take care of her.

16:23.120 --> 16:25.540
<i>Hyoma-san's "at work"...</i>

16:26.080 --> 16:27.670
<i>It feels a little strange to see.</i>

16:28.130 --> 16:32.800
Kunato-san, I can't thank you 
enough for everything.

16:32.800 --> 16:34.860
I was doing my job, nothing more.

16:35.630 --> 16:39.390
Could I say one thing? About Botan-san...

16:40.890 --> 16:44.890
She's not a normal human, is she?

16:45.440 --> 16:48.920
From my... Well, speaking as a tsukumogami...

16:48.920 --> 16:53.400
I feel a warmth toward her 
akin to what I feel for my master.

16:54.160 --> 16:55.870
Be careful.

16:55.870 --> 17:00.380
There will be no lack of moths 
drawn to that light.

17:01.470 --> 17:05.170
Please protect that dear girl.

17:05.480 --> 17:08.920
I will. I'm a Saenome.

17:12.000 --> 17:13.050
Hey...

17:13.440 --> 17:15.660
Thanks for taking me along today.

17:15.660 --> 17:18.050
It's been kind of educational, 
in a few different ways.

17:18.440 --> 17:19.450
Educational?

17:19.450 --> 17:20.300
Yeah.

17:26.230 --> 17:31.570
I haven't talked much with tsukumogami 
other than the ones in my household.

17:32.220 --> 17:37.530
I never knew they had so many 
different ways of feeling and being.

17:37.900 --> 17:40.360
What a coincidence. I felt the same way.

17:40.360 --> 17:41.140
Huh?

17:41.620 --> 17:45.500
But don't Saenome specialize in tsukumogami?

17:45.500 --> 17:50.240
Well... I always sealed them on sight.

17:50.240 --> 17:53.380
I never saw any reason to hear them out.

17:53.760 --> 17:55.770
<i>What a problem child!</i>

17:56.810 --> 17:58.040
Hey, Hyoma-san.

17:58.040 --> 17:59.690
Can I ask you one question?

17:59.690 --> 18:02.580
Yes. I'll answer as best I can.

18:04.390 --> 18:09.150
Why are you so hard on tsukumogami?

18:12.160 --> 18:14.150
Haori never told you?

18:14.960 --> 18:16.630
Does Haori know?

18:17.380 --> 18:19.750
It's quite simple.

18:20.600 --> 18:24.040
My brother and sister were 
killed by a tsukumogami.

18:25.200 --> 18:27.210
I was twelve years old at the time.

18:27.210 --> 18:29.380
My twin siblings were eighteen.

18:30.120 --> 18:33.830
They were already working as Saenome, 
as successors to the Kunato leadership.

18:34.920 --> 18:39.990
My sister's name was Kusui. 
She was like a mother to me, and very kind.

18:40.550 --> 18:41.990
My brother was Hayato.

18:42.520 --> 18:44.660
He was acknowledged by all as a prodigy,

18:44.660 --> 18:47.180
and my teacher in combat techniques.

18:48.280 --> 18:56.230
And their killer was a tsukumogami wandering 
the streets whom they'd come to save.

18:57.340 --> 19:01.940
The sight of that tsukumogami, laughing as
 it speared them both on its skewers...

19:03.760 --> 19:06.040
I can't purge it from my mind.

19:09.010 --> 19:12.290
I'm sorry. I asked so carelessly...

19:12.290 --> 19:15.510
No matter. I should have told you in advance.

19:16.320 --> 19:19.460
When I left to join your household, 
my grandfather told me,

19:19.980 --> 19:22.730
"See, for the first time, 
the nature of tsukumogami."

19:23.650 --> 19:26.310
See their nature?

19:27.160 --> 19:29.310
There are many kinds of tsukumogami.

19:29.310 --> 19:32.710
It's just as you said earlier.

19:33.320 --> 19:37.980
It's possible understanding that is
how I'll be able to move forward.

19:39.700 --> 19:41.950
I'm starting to internalize it...

19:42.280 --> 19:43.270
That Yagen

19:43.820 --> 19:45.840
and the Nagatsuki tsukumogami

19:46.640 --> 19:48.810
are nothing like that paper umbrella.

19:49.660 --> 19:50.630
But...

19:51.150 --> 19:52.380
You can change.

19:53.850 --> 19:59.090
You already come off really differently 
than you did when I first met you.

19:59.450 --> 20:03.840
You're a lot more gentle with 
my people and with Yagen-san.

20:04.460 --> 20:07.450
Early on, I thought you'd give me an ulcer.

20:08.770 --> 20:10.430
Forgive me.

20:11.400 --> 20:13.830
What you're saying seems rather unreal to me.

20:15.590 --> 20:18.440
Then let me give you my guarantee.

20:18.440 --> 20:21.440
You can change. You can overcome this.

20:24.260 --> 20:26.100
I know you can.

20:27.800 --> 20:31.450
You know I speak with authority, right?

20:31.840 --> 20:32.580
Right?

20:37.030 --> 20:39.370
If you give me your endorsement,

20:39.370 --> 20:41.270
I'll endeavor to live up to it.

20:42.090 --> 20:43.770
Can't wait to see it.

20:44.580 --> 20:46.720
<i>I still feel them...</i>

20:46.720 --> 20:50.180
<i>The eyes of the tsukumogami 
just looking this way.</i>

20:51.100 --> 20:54.570
<i>And on the far bank, 
a presence holding it at bay...</i>

20:57.920 --> 20:59.610
<i>And one spike of hostility directed at me?!</i>

21:00.140 --> 21:01.680
Don't be mean, Yu.

21:01.680 --> 21:02.610
Seriously.

21:02.610 --> 21:05.390
But they're on a d-date!

21:05.390 --> 21:07.120
They're just on a walk.

21:07.120 --> 21:10.640
Botan's far too young to be 
walking alone with a man!

21:10.640 --> 21:13.870
How old do you think she is?

21:14.160 --> 21:15.180
What's wrong?

21:15.750 --> 21:17.930
It's truly an overwhelming atmosphere.

21:17.930 --> 21:19.750
You never fail to amaze me, Nagatsuki-san.

21:20.640 --> 21:21.980
Oh, that's right!

21:21.980 --> 21:23.370
About that...

21:23.370 --> 21:24.630
Call me Botan!

21:25.520 --> 21:28.120
"Nagatsuki-san" could refer 
to any of my people.

21:28.520 --> 21:31.760
And my friends all call me by my given name.

21:31.760 --> 21:34.770
Y-You are certain? P-Perhaps...

21:34.770 --> 21:36.600
Call her by her given name?!

21:36.600 --> 21:39.040
It's indecent! Utterly indecent!

21:37.920 --> 21:40.020
We're going home, Yu!

21:41.110 --> 21:42.030
Try and say it.

21:42.030 --> 21:44.780
E-Er... isn't that a bit sudden?

21:44.780 --> 21:46.680
Come on, for practice!

21:47.720 --> 21:49.100
Go on, do it!

21:49.560 --> 21:51.560
B... B-B...

21:51.560 --> 21:53.340
I can't hear you!

23:25.000 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

23:25.000 --> 23:40.020
<b>Fire</b>
